(235109, 13930, 6451, '<td valign="top">Very nice image and reflection as well.  The sky also looks dark and then fades to a lighter color which creates a nice range of lighting for the image. But where is the bridge in the image??</td>', 'Very nice image and reflection as well.  The sky also looks dark and then fades to a lighter color which creates a nice range of lighting for the image. But where is the bridge in the image??', '2003-03-11 14:20:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(235110, 13825, 772, '<td valign="top">This is definitely a beautiful scene.  With ''bridges'' being the theme of the challenge, maybe a closer view of the bridge itself would be stronger for this challenge :) - setzler</td>', 'This is definitely a beautiful scene.  With ''bridges'' being the theme of the challenge, maybe a closer view of the bridge itself would be stronger for this challenge :) - setzler', '2003-03-11 14:24:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(235111, 13543, 772, '<td valign="top">I like the mysterious feel and the nice contrast in this photo... excellent work :)</td>', 'I like the mysterious feel and the nice contrast in this photo... excellent work :)', '2003-03-11 14:28:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(235112, 13683, 772, '<td valign="top">very nice work... the sense of motion is strong in this shot... great idea :) - setzler</td>', 'very nice work... the sense of motion is strong in this shot... great idea :) - setzler', '2003-03-11 14:28:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(235113, 13745, 772, '<td valign="top">the smooth curve in this photo works very well... the misty/foggy weather seems to offer a nice sense of serenity in this shot as well... nice work :) - setzler</td>', 'the smooth curve in this photo works very well... the misty/foggy weather seems to offer a nice sense of serenity in this shot as well... nice work :) - setzler', '2003-03-11 14:29:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(235114, 13778, 772, '<td valign="top">I like the lines in this photo.. the walkway bridge looks interesting as well, but I think it''s framed just a tiny bit too close to the top of the frame... maybe a little extra breathing room up there would be nice also.. nice work :) - setzler</td>', 'I like the lines in this photo.. the walkway bridge looks interesting as well, but I think it''s framed just a tiny bit too close to the top of the frame... maybe a little extra breathing room up there would be nice also.. nice work :) - setzler', '2003-03-11 14:31:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(235116, 13652, 772, '<td valign="top">This is a nice architectural shot.. the lines and diagonals are excellent.. In my opinion, this is not the best photo for a ''bridge'' theme because the bridge is not visible in the photo.  What we see here doesn''t really prepresent a ''bridge''... - setzler</td>', 'This is a nice architectural shot.. the lines and diagonals are excellent.. In my opinion, this is not the best photo for a ''bridge'' theme because the bridge is not visible in the photo.  What we see here doesn''t really prepresent a ''bridge''... - setzler', '2003-03-11 14:32:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(235117, 13641, 772, '<td valign="top">very interesting alternative view of the bridge challenge... the composition is excellent... great shot :) - setzler</td>', 'very interesting alternative view of the bridge challenge... the composition is excellent... great shot :) - setzler', '2003-03-11 14:33:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(235121, 13930, 656, '<td valign="top">bridge really feels like a secondary element in this - almost impossible to see and the shot is dominated by the skyline/reflection, not the bridge.</td>', 'bridge really feels like a secondary element in this - almost impossible to see and the shot is dominated by the skyline/reflection, not the bridge.', '2003-03-11 14:46:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(235127, 13592, 6328, '<td valign="top">What a beautiful bridge.  That stark white sure stands out amongst the greens and the yellow flowers on the left, and I sure like the reflections on the poles in the water. I just wonder if you had stepped back a few feet and included the bench on the right,would it have been too crowed? Or come over to your left and taken it out altogether?   All in all, it doesn''t matter, you''ve got a lovely photograph, nice and crisp, sharp focus, good colours.</td>', 'What a beautiful bridge.  That stark white sure stands out amongst the greens and the yellow flowers on the left, and I sure like the reflections on the poles in the water. I just wonder if you had stepped back a few feet and included the bench on the right,would it have been too crowed? Or come over to your left and taken it out altogether?   All in all, it doesn''t matter, you''ve got a lovely photograph, nice and crisp, sharp focus, good colours.', '2003-03-11 15:09:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(235128, 13697, 6328, '<td valign="top">Great shot of the two bridges, nice colours too, I like the concrete bases on the old one with the different colours in them, and then of course the stark white/gray of the concrete of the new bridge with the shadows from the older bridge.  Nice job.</td>', 'Great shot of the two bridges, nice colours too, I like the concrete bases on the old one with the different colours in them, and then of course the stark white/gray of the concrete of the new bridge with the shadows from the older bridge.  Nice job.', '2003-03-11 15:13:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(235130, 13793, 6328, '<td valign="top">Got to be honest with you, I think you had a great enough photo without the umbrella.  I like the way you caught the moss on the wood in front of your camera and the way the rails lead right down under the bridge is great.  Was there any way of showing slightly more of the bridge?<br/>Your photo is nice and clear, it''s crisp, sharp, and in focus, but that umbrella really bothers me.</td>', 'Got to be honest with you, I think you had a great enough photo without the umbrella.  I like the way you caught the moss on the wood in front of your camera and the way the rails lead right down under the bridge is great.  Was there any way of showing slightly more of the bridge?Your photo is nice and clear, it''s crisp, sharp, and in focus, but that umbrella really bothers me.', '2003-03-11 15:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(235132, 13650, 6328, '<td valign="top">Hi.  I really like the colours on this bridge.  The way you shot up into it is very different and the blue sky adds a nice touch to the overall photograph.  I just can''t imagine the work that went into building something like this.  I mean, just look at the brickwork, the arches, those street lamps look great, and you''ve captured those railings against the blue sky just perfectly.<br/>I wonder had you waited just another 1/2 hour or so, if the sun shining down on the frozen water, if the reflection would have lit up the inside of the (tunnels) very much to show more details?  Doesn''t matter.  Great shot. Congratulations!</td>', 'Hi.  I really like the colours on this bridge.  The way you shot up into it is very different and the blue sky adds a nice touch to the overall photograph.  I just can''t imagine the work that went into building something like this.  I mean, just look at the brickwork, the arches, those street lamps look great, and you''ve captured those railings against the blue sky just perfectly.I wonder had you waited just another 1/2 hour or so, if the sun shining down on the frozen water, if the reflection would have lit up the inside of the (tunnels) very much to show more details?  Doesn''t matter.  Great shot. Congratulations!', '2003-03-11 15:22:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(235133, 13668, 6328, '<td valign="top">You/ve captured a really nice shot of this footbridge with the towers on either side.  My only complaint is that the sky is just a mite too bright - - any way you could have toned it down a bit??</td>', 'You/ve captured a really nice shot of this footbridge with the towers on either side.  My only complaint is that the sky is just a mite too bright - - any way you could have toned it down a bit??', '2003-03-11 15:25:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(235135, 13825, 1005, '<td valign="top">Pretty scene, strong contrasts between the trees and the snow.  The bridge seems a little far away, but is definately the subject.  The snow falling is pretty in person, but tends to look more like grain in the photo.  5 Swash</td>', 'Pretty scene, strong contrasts between the trees and the snow.  The bridge seems a little far away, but is definately the subject.  The snow falling is pretty in person, but tends to look more like grain in the photo.  5 Swash', '2003-03-11 15:29:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(235136, 13917, 6328, '<td valign="top">Really nice photograph.  I like looking at the steel and wood bridges.  Can I be a bit honest with you?    What if you waited almost until dark when perhaps there was more dramatic lighting in the sky?  Shot it a little to the left or right instead of dead centre?</td>', 'Really nice photograph.  I like looking at the steel and wood bridges.  Can I be a bit honest with you?    What if you waited almost until dark when perhaps there was more dramatic lighting in the sky?  Shot it a little to the left or right instead of dead centre?', '2003-03-11 15:32:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(235137, 13735, 1005, '<td valign="top">Well, the lavender is eye catchy.....You have major border problems (hint:  draw a solid line around your picture first (stops the paint bucket bleed), then create your border with paint fill.  Photo in general seems less than sharp, but could be partly due to the color manip.  5 Swash</td>', 'Well, the lavender is eye catchy.....You have major border problems (hint:  draw a solid line around your picture first (stops the paint bucket bleed), then create your border with paint fill.  Photo in general seems less than sharp, but could be partly due to the color manip.  5 Swash', '2003-03-11 15:34:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(235138, 13608, 1005, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot!  This view makes the span look longer than it really is.  Some of the detail in the distance (islands/trees) aren\''t very clear, but the bridge is!  Very good color!  9 Swash<br/>*BTW - title is fairly well known, but I''ll bet you''re getting some comments that don''t get it.</td>', 'Very nice shot!  This view makes the span look longer than it really is.  Some of the detail in the distance (islands/trees) aren\''t very clear, but the bridge is!  Very good color!  9 Swash*BTW - title is fairly well known, but I''ll bet you''re getting some comments that don''t get it.', '2003-03-11 15:35:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(235139, 13781, 6328, '<td valign="top">Really like the way you kept yourself to the right side of the bridge to take your shot.  So many people shoot from dead centre.  I like the shadows created on the roadway by the afternoon sun.  The only thing missing here is a girl/boy walking hand in hand way down at the other end.  You''ve got some nice tones here for a B&amp;W and I like the way the rivets are so clear on the beam to the right side.</td>', 'Really like the way you kept yourself to the right side of the bridge to take your shot.  So many people shoot from dead centre.  I like the shadows created on the roadway by the afternoon sun.  The only thing missing here is a girl/boy walking hand in hand way down at the other end.  You''ve got some nice tones here for a B&W and I like the way the rivets are so clear on the beam to the right side.', '2003-03-11 15:35:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(235143, 13953, 1005, '<td valign="top">Pretty picture.... is the challenge aspect a metaphore? (I don''t see any "bridge" in the frame.)  The bricks took the sepia well, but not so good for the wood siding.  <br/>5 Swash</td>', 'Pretty picture.... is the challenge aspect a metaphore? (I don''t see any "bridge" in the frame.)  The bricks took the sepia well, but not so good for the wood siding.  5 Swash', '2003-03-11 15:42:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(235145, 13778, 6328, '<td valign="top">Wow, what a busy scene you''ve captured.  I almost wish there was an engine rushing towards me. . .  You''ve got a lot of detail on those rails and ties, the road sign, the sign on the bridge, the grease on the tracks.  You''ve got good gray tones too.  Nice photograph.</td>', 'Wow, what a busy scene you''ve captured.  I almost wish there was an engine rushing towards me. . .  You''ve got a lot of detail on those rails and ties, the road sign, the sign on the bridge, the grease on the tracks.  You''ve got good gray tones too.  Nice photograph.', '2003-03-11 15:42:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(235148, 13918, 1005, '<td valign="top">Ummm, pushing the challenge theme a bit, but accepted (barely).  The glare on the "Taliesin" book is very harsh (try softening the light source with gauze or the like).  Color and focus seem very nice.  Why such a crooked bridge (not an engineer, eh)?  5 Swash</td>', 'Ummm, pushing the challenge theme a bit, but accepted (barely).  The glare on the "Taliesin" book is very harsh (try softening the light source with gauze or the like).  Color and focus seem very nice.  Why such a crooked bridge (not an engineer, eh)?  5 Swash', '2003-03-11 15:44:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(235151, 13944, 6328, '<td valign="top">I don''t know if I''d want to be down there with those 3 engine rumbling over top of me.  Great photograph.  Just look at the rust on those two bridge spans!  Even the trestle part of the bridge looks uncared for.  Like the way you''ve captured the yellow and black of the Engines, even the red lines of the engine 2199 and it''s Red Numbers.  Nice focus, good and crisp, sharp.  Can we talk about Noise?  I imagine there was lots of it with those 3 engines passing by! !  Congratulations on a good shot!</td>', 'I don''t know if I''d want to be down there with those 3 engine rumbling over top of me.  Great photograph.  Just look at the rust on those two bridge spans!  Even the trestle part of the bridge looks uncared for.  Like the way you''ve captured the yellow and black of the Engines, even the red lines of the engine 2199 and it''s Red Numbers.  Nice focus, good and crisp, sharp.  Can we talk about Noise?  I imagine there was lots of it with those 3 engines passing by! !  Congratulations on a good shot!', '2003-03-11 15:49:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(235153, 13665, 6328, '<td valign="top">Hi.  Nice photo.  I don''t really see anything challenging, something I might see in a holiday magazine or something.  sorry.</td>', 'Hi.  Nice photo.  I don''t really see anything challenging, something I might see in a holiday magazine or something.  sorry.', '2003-03-11 15:52:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(235154, 13552, 3037, '<td valign="top">Not that you need this comment as it''s probably oversaid..time.</td>', 'Not that you need this comment as it''s probably oversaid..time.', '2003-03-11 15:57:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(235164, 13608, 7244, '<td valign="top">Didn''t this thing fall down??</td>', 'Didn''t this thing fall down??', '2003-03-11 16:27:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(235165, 13763, 5266, '<td valign="top">Wrong!! The world''s longest covered bridge is in Hartland, New Brunswick, Canada.  And believe me, this photo was not taken in March in NB!!  Nice pic, but title is incorrect!!</td>', 'Wrong!! The world''s longest covered bridge is in Hartland, New Brunswick, Canada.  And believe me, this photo was not taken in March in NB!!  Nice pic, but title is incorrect!!', '2003-03-11 16:27:44.000000', NULL, 1),
