(235709, 13538, 2482, '<td valign="top">Nice shot, this one would of been good for the from above challenge too. The snow gives it a great crisp feel.</td>', 'Nice shot, this one would of been good for the from above challenge too. The snow gives it a great crisp feel.', '2003-03-12 00:06:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(235710, 13830, 4877, '<td valign="top">Lovely effect.  I really like your composition and effective use of lighting conditions.  Morning/evening (whichever it is) is a great time of day for this.  I would like to have seen a little more detail in the image.  Maybe this is due to compression.  Keep up the great work!</td>', 'Lovely effect.  I really like your composition and effective use of lighting conditions.  Morning/evening (whichever it is) is a great time of day for this.  I would like to have seen a little more detail in the image.  Maybe this is due to compression.  Keep up the great work!', '2003-03-12 00:07:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(235711, 13575, 4877, '<td valign="top">Very well taken!  I like your choice of bridge and the colour combinations you have used.  The spot of red in the car adds effect.  The buildings in the left, set the scene well.  Composition is great!  I dont think you could have done much better with this shot!  Great work!</td>', 'Very well taken!  I like your choice of bridge and the colour combinations you have used.  The spot of red in the car adds effect.  The buildings in the left, set the scene well.  Composition is great!  I dont think you could have done much better with this shot!  Great work!', '2003-03-12 00:09:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(235714, 13749, 4877, '<td valign="top">I really like your composition, effective use of contrast and it is great to see motion in your shot, as very few other images have an inherant motion element to them.  Like the sepia tones you have used as well.  Great work!</td>', 'I really like your composition, effective use of contrast and it is great to see motion in your shot, as very few other images have an inherant motion element to them.  Like the sepia tones you have used as well.  Great work!', '2003-03-12 00:11:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(235718, 13609, 6328, '<td valign="top">Wow.  Really nice photograph.  I like the way you''ve stood off to one side instead of taking your shot from "dead centre".  Using your imagination helps a lot, doesn''t it! !  My only thought though is why you cropped so close?  why not widen it out some more and show more of the bridge?  It''s made to be shown!  The workmanship is outstanding on a bridge like this. . .</td>', 'Wow.  Really nice photograph.  I like the way you''ve stood off to one side instead of taking your shot from "dead centre".  Using your imagination helps a lot, doesn''t it! !  My only thought though is why you cropped so close?  why not widen it out some more and show more of the bridge?  It''s made to be shown!  The workmanship is outstanding on a bridge like this. . .', '2003-03-12 00:13:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(235719, 13684, 4877, '<td valign="top">I really like the idea of having someone stand at the end of the bridge like this, gaining the silhouette effect!  Great use of leading lines.  I like the detail you have in the internal structure of the bridge.  It feels just a little off balance being that close to the left hand side of the bridge.  But overall, I think you''ve executed this one really well.</td>', 'I really like the idea of having someone stand at the end of the bridge like this, gaining the silhouette effect!  Great use of leading lines.  I like the detail you have in the internal structure of the bridge.  It feels just a little off balance being that close to the left hand side of the bridge.  But overall, I think you''ve executed this one really well.', '2003-03-12 00:15:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(235720, 13688, 6328, '<td valign="top">You''ve got a nice shot of the bridge and the couple in front of you give nice detail along with the child to the left, but did you give it this purplish tone?? Why?</td>', 'You''ve got a nice shot of the bridge and the couple in front of you give nice detail along with the child to the left, but did you give it this purplish tone?? Why?', '2003-03-12 00:18:11.000000', NULL, 1),
