(238338, 13903, 6892, '<td valign="top">Congrats! You did good kiddo. I grew up in SF you know and the Golden Gate will always have a warm spot in my heart. You caught it at its most beautiful, in the fog. Good work!</td>', 'Congrats! You did good kiddo. I grew up in SF you know and the Golden Gate will always have a warm spot in my heart. You caught it at its most beautiful, in the fog. Good work!', '2003-03-17 01:11:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(238350, 13873, 1880, '<td valign="top">Congrats on an outstanding photo. This was one of my 10s this week. Congrats on the win!!!<br/> <br/>Bob</td>', 'Congrats on an outstanding photo. This was one of my 10s this week. Congrats on the win!!! Bob', '2003-03-17 01:18:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(238366, 13748, 4877, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the great comments!  I thought I''d try out an unusual photo for my first submission.  Have learnt a lot about the voting patterns on dpchallenge.com now!  <br/> <br/>The photo was composed as-is (no cropping).  I had the camera tilted slightly to the left in order to fit in the closest section of the bridge - the right hand side.  Location is from Milsons Point - north side of the harbour, in Sydney Australia.  I set the exposure for 15 seconds, framed the "top" bridge which you see.  Set the photo off, then counted the seconds, and moved the camera roughly half way through the shot.  My camera does not display the image as I''m taking the shot, so I was guessing where it was pointed after I moved it mid-photo.  The result was quite unique.  Something I''ll try next time is having some black cardboard to put in front of the lense as I''m moving it to remove the light streaks, just to see how it would have come out.  Post photo edit consisted of a change in hue/saturation to give the blue/purple colour, enhancing the mood.</td>', 'Thanks for all the great comments!  I thought I''d try out an unusual photo for my first submission.  Have learnt a lot about the voting patterns on dpchallenge.com now!   The photo was composed as-is (no cropping).  I had the camera tilted slightly to the left in order to fit in the closest section of the bridge - the right hand side.  Location is from Milsons Point - north side of the harbour, in Sydney Australia.  I set the exposure for 15 seconds, framed the "top" bridge which you see.  Set the photo off, then counted the seconds, and moved the camera roughly half way through the shot.  My camera does not display the image as I''m taking the shot, so I was guessing where it was pointed after I moved it mid-photo.  The result was quite unique.  Something I''ll try next time is having some black cardboard to put in front of the lense as I''m moving it to remove the light streaks, just to see how it would have come out.  Post photo edit consisted of a change in hue/saturation to give the blue/purple colour, enhancing the mood.', '2003-03-17 01:30:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(238370, 13551, 6458, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments and the voting.  <br/> <br/>I almost didn''t submit this because of the barbed wire.. It bothered me so much that I debated going down late at night and cutting it out, just so I could take the shot properly. My good sense got the better of me and I decided that a blue ribbon wouldn''t help much with the barrister''s fees if I got caught. ;)<br/> <br/>Does DPC have a legal fund set up for it''s members?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-03-17 07:42:21.</i></td>', 'Thanks for the comments and the voting.   I almost didn''t submit this because of the barbed wire.. It bothered me so much that I debated going down late at night and cutting it out, just so I could take the shot properly. My good sense got the better of me and I decided that a blue ribbon wouldn''t help much with the barrister''s fees if I got caught. ;) Does DPC have a legal fund set up for it''s members?', '2003-03-17 01:37:56.000000', '2003-03-17 07:42:21.000000', 0),
(238374, 13653, 1360, '<td valign="top">I think this picture could have been a lot better with some more dramatic lighting.  <br/>I bet, at sunset, if the golden sun shone on the pylons, for instance, it would be a much more strinking shot.<br/> <br/></td>', 'I think this picture could have been a lot better with some more dramatic lighting.  I bet, at sunset, if the golden sun shone on the pylons, for instance, it would be a much more strinking shot. ', '2003-03-17 01:43:39.000000', NULL, 0),
